      note: the formula of the equation of centre, p. 22
    - ref: fr:kepler-sec/Swerdlow2026/0052/p05
      role: witness
      note: Ptolemy's values and the maximum equation, p. 22
    - ref: fr:kepler-sec/Swerdlow2026/0052/p06
      role: witness
      note: al-Battānī's values, p. 22
    - ref: fr:kepler-sec/Swerdlow2026/0047/p03
      role: witness
      note: source of the year T = 365;14,48
    work: Ptolemy's solar model, in its eccentric and its epicyclic form, as Noel Swerdlow uses it in The Renaissance
      of Astronomy (2026), chapter 1
    edition: Famulus collection kepler-sec, document Swerdlow2026 (scan page n is printed page n − 30 in chapter
      1)
    method: The language astra/1 writes a model, its parametrisations, a superposition, figures and derivations
      as texts of their own kinds, each with its own check. The case study writes eighteen such texts from Swerdlow's
      pages on Ptolemy's solar model and reports what the checks found.
    limits:
    - 'A derivation that passes the four checks is not a formal proof in an axiomatic system: truth is tested on
      samples, rules are matched as schemas, configuration conditions are evaluated numerically.'
    - Cases have to be found by the author of a derivation; the checks do not propose the distinction.
    - Hypotheses have to fix a parameter; inequalities between parameters and hypotheses of incidence are not supported.
    - The grades 'read off the construction' and 'calculation' are tested numerically and not replayed symbolically;
      an expansion is tested at three sizes of the small ratio.
    - The language is planar; motions taken from tables are not implemented; only the solar model is written.
    - The level 'attested' checks that a source is named, not that it says what the parametrisation says.
    - The Almagest is not among the addressable texts; the attribution to Ptolemy and the loci in the Almagest are
      as Swerdlow's page gives them.
    - The propositions of Euclid are cited by the page of Heath's translation, not by paragraph.
    - The code is not yet public.
